**Subject:** Next LivSCt@RI meeting: Thursday 4th June @ 14.30 Rm 1-003 " Ubiquitin and regulation of mitochondrial health"

Dear Colleagues,

Im excited to announce that the next LivSCt@RI meeting on Thursday 4th June @14.30 in Rm 1-003 will be a talk given by Professor Mike Clague from the Institute of Systems, Molecular & Integrative Biology at University of Liverpool. Mike is an internationally renowned, leading expert in studying membrane trafficking (endocytosis, autophagy, mitochondrial dynamics) and cell signaling: focusing on mechanisms that lead to cancer and neurodegeneration (Parkinson's Disease). His lab also has a particularly strong interest in the deubiquitylase (DUB) family of enzymes ([https://pcwww.liv.ac.uk/\~clague/](https://pcwww.liv.ac.uk/%7Eclague/)). 

The title of Mike’s talk is:

“Ubiquitin and regulation of mitochondrial health”

From my informal chats with colleagues, I know there are already a few folk who would like to have an opportunity to chat with Mike 1:1 during his visit. **If you are interested in talking to Mike – please let me know in the next 10 days, so I can organise a meeting schedule when I return from leave on the 28th May.**

As always we encourage in person attendance, however for those who cant make it a TEAMs invite will be sent at the end of next week.

Best wishes

Tom

